{%- comment -%}
  ─── BACK ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  A real control, not a reliance on the browser's own Back button (a shopper
  who arrived via a shared link, a new tab, or search has no "back" to press
  at all). `data-mc-back` is wired in marathon-storefront.js: it calls
  `history.back()` when this tab actually has somewhere of ours to go back
  TO, and falls through to a plain link otherwise — so the control never
  dead-ends. The `href` here is that fallback, resolved at RENDER time from
  `document.referrer` when JavaScript can, or the given `fallback` param when
  it can't (no-JS, or a referrer Shopify's own privacy policy stripped).

  ACCEPTS
    fallback   URL to use if there's no referrer and no history to walk back
               through — pass the sensible parent (a collection page's own
               URL, or `routes.root_url` on the product page).
    label      link text, defaults to "Back"
{%- endcomment -%}
<a class="mc-back" href="{{ fallback | default: routes.root_url }}" data-mc-back>
  <span aria-hidden="true">&larr;</span> {{ label | default: 'Back' }}
</a>
